 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 242, "q": "Folic acid supplementation is indicated in —", "opts": ["Only hereditary spherocytosis", "All children with chronic haemolytic anaemias", "Only transfusion-dependent thalassaemia", "Only after aplastic crisis"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Folic acid is given to all children with chronic haemolytic anaemias. (Book p242)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-065"},
 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 242, "q": "The best treatment modality for hereditary spherocytosis is —", "opts": ["Lifelong folic acid", "Regular transfusion", "Splenectomy", "Hydroxyurea"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Splenectomy is described as the best treatment modality. (Book p242)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-066"},
 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 242, "q": "Match each step of the benefit of splenectomy in hereditary spherocytosis with what follows it:", "opts": ["A-4, B-2, C-1, D-3", "A-2, B-4, C-3, D-1", "A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2", "A-2, B-4, C-1, D-3"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Splenectomy → ↓ lysis → ↑ RBC lifespan → ↓ severity of anaemia; gallstones are dealt with in the same sitting. Correct pairs: Splenectomy→Decreased lysis of RBCs; Decreased lysis→Increased lifespan of RBCs; Increased RBC lifespan→Decreased severity of anaemia; Gallstones present→Concomitant cholecystectomy. (Book p242)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Splenectomy", "Decreased severity of anaemia"], ["Decreased lysis", "Decreased lysis of RBCs"], ["Increased RBC lifespan", "Concomitant cholecystectomy"], ["Gallstones present", "Increased lifespan of RBCs"]], "id": "PEDS-C51-067"},
 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 242, "q": "The surgical approach preferred for splenectomy in hereditary spherocytosis is —", "opts": ["Laparoscopic partial splenectomy", "Splenic artery embolisation", "Open partial splenectomy with mesh wrap", "Open total splenectomy"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Laparoscopic partial splenectomy is preferred. (Book p242)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-068"},
 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 242, "q": "Cholecystectomy is performed along with splenectomy when —", "opts": ["The child is younger than 6 years", "Gallstones are present", "MCHC exceeds 36 g/dl", "The family history is positive"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Concomitant cholecystectomy if gallstones are present. (Book p242)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-069"},
 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 242, "q": "True or False — Splenectomy in hereditary spherocytosis corrects the underlying membrane protein defect.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — it only reduces lysis and prolongs RBC lifespan, thereby decreasing the severity of anaemia. (Book p242)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C51-070"},
 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 243, "q": "The consequence of splenectomy begins with absence of splenic ___.", "opts": ["Sinusoids", "Endothelium", "Lymphocytes", "Macrophages"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Absence of splenic macrophages → risk of infection by encapsulated bacteria. (Book p243)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C51-071"},
 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 243, "q": "Post-splenectomy patients are especially at risk of infection by —", "opts": ["Encapsulated bacteria", "Anaerobes", "Dermatophytes", "Intracellular mycobacteria"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Absence of splenic macrophages → risk of infection by encapsulated bacteria. (Book p243)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-072"},
 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 243, "q": "The risk of post-splenectomy sepsis is particularly high if the age is —", "opts": ["> 6 years", "< 6 years", "< 2 years", "> 10 years"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Risk of infection by encapsulated bacteria, especially if age < 6 yrs. (Book p243)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-073"},
