 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 243, "q": "Odd one out (organisms listed as the post-splenectomy risk):", "opts": ["Haemophilus influenzae type b", "Neisseria meningitidis", "Yersinia enterocolitica", "Streptococcus pneumoniae"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Yersinia enterocolitica is the organism linked with iron overload in thalassaemia, not the post-splenectomy encapsulated trio. (Book p243)", "type": "odd", "id": "PEDS-C51-078"},
 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 243, "q": "True or False — Immunization is one of the precautions taken around splenectomy in hereditary spherocytosis.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — precautions are surgery > 6 years, immunization, and penicillin for 2 years post surgery. (Book p243)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C51-079"},
 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 243, "q": "The most appropriate advice is —", "opts": ["Defer surgery until after 6 years of age and continue folic acid", "Avoid splenectomy altogether in this disease", "Perform splenectomy with cholecystectomy now", "Operate immediately, as splenectomy is the best treatment"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Precaution: splenectomy is best done after 6 years of age because of the risk of encapsulated-organism sepsis in younger children. (Book p243)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 4-year-old with hereditary spherocytosis has Hb 8 g/dl, splenomegaly and no gallstones; the parents ask for splenectomy now.", "id": "PEDS-C51-080"},
 {"sec": "Hereditary spherocytosis — management and splenectomy · p242–243", "page": 243, "q": "The infection to be presumed and covered first is —", "opts": ["Cytomegalovirus reactivation with hepatitis", "Encapsulated bacterial sepsis (pneumococcus, meningococcus)", "Parvovirus B19-induced aplastic crisis", "Yersinia enterocolitica enterocolitis"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Absence of splenic macrophages leaves the child at risk of overwhelming infection by encapsulated bacteria. (Book p243)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 9-year-old who underwent laparoscopic partial splenectomy 8 months ago presents with high fever and rapid deterioration.", "id": "PEDS-C51-081"},
