 {"sec": "G6PD deficiency — epidemiology and pathophysiology · p243", "page": 243, "q": "Match each component of the HMP shunt with its role as shown in the chapter:", "opts": ["A-1, B-4, C-3, D-2", "A-2, B-3, C-4, D-1", "A-3, B-2, C-4, D-1", "A-2, B-3, C-1, D-4"], "ans": 1, "exp": "The shunt sequence: G6PD → NADPH → reduced glutathione → protection; its failure → oxidative stress → haemolysis. Correct pairs: G6PD→Enzyme deficient in the disease; NADPH→Reducing equivalent generated by the shunt; Reduced glutathione→Protects RBCs from oxidative stress; Oxidative stress→Leads to haemolysis. (Book p243)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["G6PD", "Leads to haemolysis"], ["NADPH", "Enzyme deficient in the disease"], ["Reduced glutathione", "Reducing equivalent generated by the shunt"], ["Oxidative stress", "Protects RBCs from oxidative stress"]], "id": "PEDS-C51-093"},
