 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — genetics and pathogenesis · p244", "page": 244, "q": "Which of the following is listed as a trigger of sickling in an RBC containing HbS?", "opts": ["Hypothermia", "Hypercalcaemia", "Alkalosis", "Hypoxia"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Sickling triggers: hypoxia, dehydration, fever, metabolic acidosis. (Book p244)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-135"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — genetics and pathogenesis · p244", "page": 244, "q": "Along with hypoxia, dehydration and fever, ___ acidosis is listed as a trigger of sickling.", "opts": ["Metabolic", "Renal tubular", "Lactic-free", "Respiratory"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Triggers of sickling: hypoxia, dehydration, fever and metabolic acidosis. (Book p244)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C51-136"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — genetics and pathogenesis · p244", "page": 244, "q": "Repeated sickling of red cells leads to —", "opts": ["Nuclear retention", "Fragile RBCs and haemolysis", "Membrane surface area gain", "Increased deformability"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Sickling → repeated sickling → fragile RBCs → haemolysis. (Book p244)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-137"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — genetics and pathogenesis · p244", "page": 244, "q": "Sickle cells blocking blood flow in a vessel produce —", "opts": ["Iron overload", "Megaloblastic change", "Ischaemia leading to infarction", "Extramedullary haematopoiesis"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Sickle cells blocking blood flow → ischaemia → infarction. (Book p244)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-138"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — genetics and pathogenesis · p244", "page": 244, "q": "Match each element of sickle cell pathogenesis with its result:", "opts": ["A-4, B-3, C-1, D-2", "A-3, B-4, C-2, D-1", "A-2, B-1, C-4, D-3", "A-3, B-4, C-1, D-2"], "ans": 3, "exp": "The chapter's pathogenesis flow from gene mutation to vaso-occlusion. Correct pairs: Mutation in β-globin gene→Glutamate replaced by valine at position 6; Production of HbS→Sickling under hypoxia and acidosis; Repeated sickling→Fragile RBCs and haemolysis; Sickle cells blocking blood flow→Ischaemia and infarction. (Book p244)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Mutation in β-globin gene", "Fragile RBCs and haemolysis"], ["Production of HbS", "Ischaemia and infarction"], ["Repeated sickling", "Glutamate replaced by valine at position 6"], ["Sickle cells blocking blood flow", "Sickling under hypoxia and acidosis"]], "id": "PEDS-C51-139"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — genetics and pathogenesis · p244", "page": 244, "q": "True or False — Normal adult haemoglobin, against which HbS is contrasted in the chapter, is HbA.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — the book notes '(Normal Hb: HbA)' beside the production of HbS. (Book p244)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C51-140"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — genetics and pathogenesis · p244", "page": 244, "q": "True or False — Sickle cell anaemia results from a deletion of the entire β-globin gene.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — it results from a point mutation substituting valine for glutamate at the 6th position. (Book p244)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C51-141"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — genetics and pathogenesis · p244", "page": 244, "q": "Odd one out (triggers of sickling listed in the chapter):", "opts": ["Dehydration", "Fever", "Hypersplenism", "Hypoxia"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Hypersplenism is not listed; the triggers are hypoxia, dehydration, fever and metabolic acidosis. (Book p244)", "type": "odd", "id": "PEDS-C51-142"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — genetics and pathogenesis · p244", "page": 244, "q": "The molecular basis of this disorder is —", "opts": ["Deficiency of red cell G6PD with oxidative lysis", "Ankyrin gene mutation of the membrane skeleton", "Absent β-globin chain synthesis with α-chain excess", "Valine replacing glutamate at β-globin position 6"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Sickle cell anaemia — β-globin point mutation with valine for glutamate at the 6th position. (Book p244)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 3-year-old tribal child from Madhya Pradesh has recurrent painful episodes; the smear shows elongated crescent-shaped red cells.", "id": "PEDS-C51-143"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 244, "q": "Sickle cell anaemia manifests after 6 months of age because —", "opts": ["HbF predominates for 6 months and is protective", "Iron stores are exhausted at 6 months", "The spleen matures only at 6 months", "Maternal antibodies wane at 6 months"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Manifests > 6 months (HbF predominates for 6 months → protective). (Book p244)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-144"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 244, "q": "The haemoglobin that protects the infant from sickling during the first 6 months of life is ___.", "opts": ["HbA2", "HbF", "HbS", "HbA"], "ans": 1, "exp": "HbF predominates for 6 months and is protective. (Book p244)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C51-145"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 244, "q": "The crisis described as characteristic of sickle cell anaemia is —", "opts": ["Megaloblastic crisis", "Aplastic crisis", "Vaso-occlusive painful crisis", "Haemolytic crisis"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Vaso-occlusive crisis: painful episodes (characteristic). (Book p244)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-146"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 244, "q": "Dactylitis in sickle cell anaemia refers to —", "opts": ["Fusiform swelling of the wrist joint", "Digital gangrene", "Nail-bed infarction", "Swelling of the fingers and toes"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Dactylitis/hand and foot syndrome: swelling of fingers and toes. (Book p244)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-147"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 244, "q": "Dactylitis (hand-and-foot syndrome) in sickle cell anaemia typically manifests in ___.", "opts": ["Infancy", "Adolescence", "Adulthood", "The neonatal period"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Dactylitis manifests in infancy. (Book p244)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C51-148"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "Acute chest syndrome presents with —", "opts": ["Pruritic rash with expiratory wheeze", "Fever and breathing difficulty like pneumonia", "Painless gross haematuria", "Isolated periumbilical abdominal pain"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Acute chest syndrome: fever & breathing difficulty, resembles pneumonia. (Book p245)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-149"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "The chest X-ray in acute chest syndrome shows —", "opts": ["A miliary pattern", "Hyperinflation with flattened diaphragms", "New-onset infiltrates", "Bilateral hilar lymphadenopathy"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Chest X-ray shows new-onset infiltrates. (Book p245)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-150"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "Which neurological complication is listed among the clinical features of sickle cell anaemia?", "opts": ["Peripheral neuropathy", "Subacute combined degeneration", "Gelastic seizures", "Stroke episodes"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Stroke episodes are listed among the features. (Book p245)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-151"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "Repeated splenic infarcts in sickle cell anaemia lead to autosplenectomy by —", "opts": ["6 years of age", "10 years of age", "Adolescence", "2 years of age"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Repeated infarcts → autosplenectomy by 6 years of age (functional hyposplenism). (Book p245)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-152"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "Autosplenectomy in sickle cell anaemia produces functional ___.", "opts": ["Hypersplenism", "Hyposplenism", "Asplenia with regeneration", "Splenic sequestration"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Repeated infarcts → autosplenectomy → functional hyposplenism. (Book p245)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C51-153"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "The infective consequence of autosplenectomy in sickle cell anaemia is —", "opts": ["Chronic viral hepatitis with cirrhosis", "Recurrent pulmonary tuberculosis", "Recurrent infection by encapsulated bacteria", "Recurrent invasive fungal infection"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Functional hyposplenism → recurrent infection by encapsulated bacteria. (Book p245)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-154"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "Venous blockade in splenic sequestration causes —", "opts": ["Bone marrow fibrosis", "Iron overload", "Chronic microcytic anaemia", "Acute pooling of blood in the spleen"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Venous blockade → acute pooling of blood. (Book p245)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-155"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "Acute pooling of blood in the spleen causes a Hb reduction of at least ___%, leading to pallor and shock.", "opts": ["2", "5", "0.5", "1"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Venous blockade → acute pooling of blood → ≥ 2% Hb reduction → pallor, shock. (Book p245)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C51-156"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "Aplastic crisis in sickle cell anaemia is —", "opts": ["A reticulocytosis with jaundice", "Pancytopenia precipitated by parvovirus B19 infection", "Isolated neutropenia from hypersplenism", "Thrombocytosis after autosplenectomy"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Aplastic crisis: pancytopenia (precipitated by parvovirus B19 infection). (Book p245)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-157"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "Match each sickle cell complication with its description:", "opts": ["A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4", "A-2, B-4, C-1, D-3", "A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2", "A-1, B-3, C-4, D-2"], "ans": 2, "exp": "These are the four clinical presentations detailed in the chapter. Correct pairs: Vaso-occlusive crisis→Painful episodes — characteristic; Dactylitis→Swelling of fingers and toes in infancy; Acute chest syndrome→Fever, breathlessness and new infiltrates on X-ray; Aplastic crisis→Pancytopenia after parvovirus B19. (Book p244–245)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Vaso-occlusive crisis", "Swelling of fingers and toes in infancy"], ["Dactylitis", "Pancytopenia after parvovirus B19"], ["Acute chest syndrome", "Painful episodes — characteristic"], ["Aplastic crisis", "Fever, breathlessness and new infiltrates on X-ray"]], "id": "PEDS-C51-158"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "Match each consequence of splenic sickling with its mechanism:", "opts": ["A-3, B-2, C-4, D-1", "A-2, B-3, C-1, D-4", "A-1, B-4, C-3, D-2", "A-2, B-3, C-4, D-1"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Sickling in the spleen produces both chronic loss of function and acute sequestration. Correct pairs: Autosplenectomy by 6 years→Repeated splenic infarcts; Recurrent encapsulated bacterial infection→Functional hyposplenism; Acute pooling of blood in the spleen→Venous blockade; Pallor and shock→≥ 2% reduction in haemoglobin. (Book p245)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Autosplenectomy by 6 years", "≥ 2% reduction in haemoglobin"], ["Recurrent encapsulated bacterial infection", "Repeated splenic infarcts"], ["Acute pooling of blood in the spleen", "Functional hyposplenism"], ["Pallor and shock", "Venous blockade"]], "id": "PEDS-C51-159"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "True or False — Icterus and pallor are both listed among the clinical features of sickle cell anaemia.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — the feature list opens with icterus and pallor. (Book p244)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C51-160"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "True or False — Splenomegaly persisting into adult life is expected in sickle cell anaemia because of chronic haemolysis.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — repeated infarcts cause autosplenectomy by 6 years of age with functional hyposplenism. (Book p245)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C51-161"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "Odd one out (features of sickle cell anaemia described in the chapter):", "opts": ["Acute chest syndrome", "Dactylitis", "Frontal bossing with thalassemic facies", "Vaso-occlusive painful crisis"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Thalassemic facies with frontal bossing belongs to β-thalassaemia major, not sickle cell anaemia. (Book p244–246)", "type": "odd", "id": "PEDS-C51-162"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "This presentation is best described as —", "opts": ["Splenic sequestration crisis", "Parvovirus aplastic crisis", "Acute chest syndrome", "Dactylitis (hand-and-foot syndrome)"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Dactylitis — swelling of fingers and toes — manifests in infancy. (Book p244)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 9-month-old with known sickle cell disease has painful, swollen fingers and toes with low-grade fever.", "id": "PEDS-C51-163"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "The diagnosis and the specific transfusion strategy indicated are —", "opts": ["Acute chest syndrome — exchange transfusion", "Aplastic crisis — PRBC transfusion", "Splenic sequestration — exchange transfusion", "Pneumonia — simple PRBC transfusion"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Acute chest syndrome resembles pneumonia; exchange transfusion is indicated for acute chest syndrome and stroke. (Book p245)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 7-year-old with sickle cell anaemia develops fever, chest pain and breathlessness; the chest X-ray shows new infiltrates.", "id": "PEDS-C51-164"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — clinical features · p244–245", "page": 245, "q": "The mechanism responsible is —", "opts": ["Autosplenectomy from repeated infarcts", "Venous blockade with acute pooling of blood in the spleen", "Parvovirus B19 marrow suppression", "Iron overload cardiotoxicity"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Venous blockade → acute pooling of blood → ≥ 2% Hb reduction → pallor, shock. (Book p245)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 4-year-old with sickle cell anaemia becomes suddenly pale and shocked; the spleen has enlarged rapidly and the Hb has dropped sharply.", "id": "PEDS-C51-165"},
 {"sec": "Sickle cell anaemia — investigations and trait · p245", "page": 245, "q": "The peripheral smear finding in sickle cell anaemia is —", "opts": ["Schistocytes", "Spherocytes", "Sickled RBCs", "Target cells only"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Peripheral smear: sickled RBCs. (Book p245)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C51-166"},
