 {"sec": "β-thalassaemia — pathophysiology and clinical features · p246", "page": 246, "q": "Early destruction of unstable red cell precursors in β-thalassaemia is termed ___ erythropoiesis.", "opts": ["Ineffective", "Sideroblastic", "Extramedullary", "Megaloblastic"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Instability of cells → early destruction → ineffective erythropoiesis. (Book p246)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C51-216"},
